course: dictionary
lesson: 6144
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «The crushed cane stems left over are burned to power the sugar mills.» Here a mill is a factory with machines that grind and make things, not a place that makes you grind your teeth. Read the whole sentence to find which meaning fits.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «Mill Lane win 2–1 and Sam scores.» Mill Lane has a capital letter and sits in a football score, so it is a name, not a building or a machine. Names begin with capitals, and they are not in the dictionary as ordinary words.
explain: Some words sit inside phrases, and the phrase has its own meaning. «He had to go through the mill» does not mean he walked through a building. It means he had a hard time. Always check the words next to the word you don't know.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A word can have more than one meaning, so always check which one fits the sentence.
fact: «Mill» can mean a building with machines for grinding grain into flour, often powered by wind or water.
fact: «Mill» can also mean a factory where things like cotton, paper or steel are made, as in the cotton mills of the Industrial Revolution.
fact: «Run-of-the-mill» means ordinary, and «go through the mill» means have a hard time. «Mill around» means move about in a crowd without going anywhere special.
exercise: «The crushed cane stems left over are burned to power the sugar mills.» What is a sugar mill? | A sweet cake from the shop | A bridge over a river | A pepper pot on the table | *A factory with machines that grind and process cane
exercise: «He is a run-of-the-mill player, nothing special.» What does run-of-the-mill mean? | Very famous | Very large | Wet through | *Ordinary
exercise: «The shoppers began to mill around the sale table.» What does mill around mean? | Shout loudly at the cashier | *Move about in a crowd without going anywhere special | Sit very still and quiet | Grind grain into flour
test: «Water from the river turned the wheel of the old mill.» What powered the old mill? | A battery | *Water | Sunshine from a window | A pony in a field
test: «After the bad year, he had to go through the mill before he got a job.» What does go through the mill mean? | Win a race | Walk through a building | Get a free meal | *Have a hard time
exam: «The cook turned the pepper mill over the soup.» What is a pepper mill? | *A small machine for grinding pepper | A type of boat | A big factory | A place to sell soup
